### **Configuration Pattern 3: Filter Persistence**

**FilterPersistenceBridge.tsx** (lines 1-64) manages automatic filter loading:

```typescript
const STORAGE_KEY = 'inventory.filters'
const SKIP_AUTOLOAD_KEY = 'inventory.skipAutoload'

const applyFilters = () => {
  if (appliedRef.current || !searchParams) return

  const current = Object.fromEntries(searchParams.entries())
  const allowlist = new Set(['page', 'pageSize', 'orderBy'])
  const hasFilters = Object.keys(current).some(k => k.startsWith('filterBy_') || allowlist.has(k))
  if (hasFilters) return

  const raw = localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY)
  if (!raw) return

  const saved = JSON.parse(raw) as Record<string, string>
  const qp = new URLSearchParams(searchParams.toString())

  for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(saved)) {
    if (!v) continue
    if (k.startsWith('filterBy_') || allowlist.has(k)) {
      qp.set(k, v)
    }
  }

  qp.set('page', '1')
  replace(`${pathname}?${qp.toString()}`)
}
```

**Key features**:
- Filters stored in localStorage by key (filterBy_<fieldname>)
- Auto-loaded on page navigation
- Skip one-shot flag prevents loading after clear action
- Only applies if no filters already in URL

