## Q49: Relationship Between BarrelOwnershipService and GroupTransaction for Ownership Transfer Tracking

**BarrelOwnershipService** and **GroupTransaction** form a two-layer audit pattern for ownership transfers: BarrelOwnershipService orchestrates individual ownership changes while GroupTransaction groups multiple related changes into logical business operations for holistic tracking and reconciliation.

### Data Model Relationships

**apps/whk-wms/prisma/schema.prisma (lines 1450-1488, 1646-1690)**

Two complementary transaction models track ownership changes:

```prisma
model OwnershipTransaction {
  // Individual barrel ownership change
  id                    String  @id
  transactionType       EnumOwnershipTransactionType  // TRANSFER, JOINT_ESTABLISHMENT, etc.
  barrelId              String  // Which barrel changed hands
  fromCustomerId        String? // Previous owner
  toCustomerId          String? // New owner
  ownershipPercentage   Decimal // Transferred amount

  // Grouped under a business operation
  groupId               String? // Links to GroupTransaction.id
  operationId           String? // Bulk operation identifier
  batchId               String? // Batch identifier within operation

  // Audit trail
  executedBy            String
  executedAt            DateTime
  isReversed            Boolean

  // Relationships
  barrel                Barrel
  fromCustomer          Customer?  @relation("OwnershipTransactionFrom")
  toCustomer            Customer?  @relation("OwnershipTransactionTo")
  group                 OwnershipTransactionGroup?
}

model GroupTransaction {
  // High-level business operation grouping
  id                    String  @id
  transactionType       EnumGroupTransactionType  // ADJUSTMENT, OWNERSHIP_TRANSFER, etc.
  status                EnumGroupTransactionStatus  // PENDING, COMPLETED, etc.

  // Which barrels were affected in this operation
  affectedBarrelIds     String[]  // Array of barrel IDs touched by this transaction

  // Contextual metadata
  metadata              Json?   // Stores operation filters, batch info
  notes                 String?
  reference             String?

  // Execution tracking
  executionDate         DateTime
  completedAt           DateTime?
  executedBy            String?
  approvedBy            String?
  approvalDate          DateTime?

  // Reconciliation linkage
  reconciliationId      String?

  // Optional lot-level tracking
  trackingMode          TransactionTrackingMode  // BARREL_LEVEL or LOT_LEVEL
  lotId                 String?
  lotQuantityUnits      Decimal?
}
```

### How BarrelOwnershipService Creates GroupTransactions

**apps/whk-wms/src/barrelOwnership/barrelOwnership.service.ts (lines 140-165)**

Each batch operation creates a GroupTransaction that logically groups related OwnershipTransactions:

```typescript
private async createTransactionGroup(
  transactionType: EnumGroupTransactionType,  // ADJUSTMENT, OWNERSHIP_TRANSFER, etc.
  executedBy: string,
  data: {
    fromCustomerId?: string;
    toCustomerId?: string;
    transferReasonId?: string;
    notes?: string;
    operationId?: string;
    batchId?: string;
    metadata?: Prisma.InputJsonValue;
  },
) {
  return this.prisma.groupTransaction.create({
    data: {
      id: createId(),
      transactionType,
      executedBy,
      executionDate: new Date(),
      affectedBarrelIds: [],  // Populated later as barrels are processed
      notes: data.notes,
      metadata: data.metadata,  // Stores operation filters, batch info
      createdBy: executedBy,
    },
  });
}
