## Q51: How BarrelOwnershipService.getBulkBarrelOwnerships Optimizes Fetching Multiple Barrel Ownerships

The **getBulkBarrelOwnerships** method optimizes multi-barrel ownership fetching through a **single batched database query** that reduces N+1 query problems and prevents connection pool exhaustion.

### Core Optimization: Single Batched Query

**apps/whk-wms/src/barrelOwnership/barrelOwnership.service.ts (lines 982-1004)**

```typescript
async getBulkBarrelOwnerships(barrelIds: string[], activeOnly: boolean = true) {
  // Guard: Return early for empty arrays (avoids unnecessary queries)
  if (barrelIds.length === 0) {
    return [];
  }

  // KEY OPTIMIZATION: Single query with { in: barrelIds } instead of loop
  const ownerships = await this.prisma.barrelOwnership.findMany({
    where: {
      barrelId: { in: barrelIds },  // Batches all barrel IDs into ONE query
      ...(activeOnly && { validTo: null }),
    },
    include: {
      customer: true,  // Eager-load customer to avoid separate queries
      barrel: true,    // Eager-load barrel to avoid separate queries
    },
    orderBy: { validFrom: "desc" },  // Most recent ownership first
  });

  // Post-processing normalization (cheap operation on fetched data)
  return ownerships.map(ownership => ({
    ...ownership,
    ownershipType: this.normalizeOwnershipType(ownership.ownershipType as string),
  }));
}
```

**Contrast with Single-Barrel Version** (lines 958-976):

