**Rate limit tiers explained:**
- **short (10/s)**: Protects against request floods from single clients. Violating this indicates a misbehaving client or DDoS attempt.
- **medium (50/10s)**: Sustainable rate for legitimate heavy users. Dashboard queries and bulk operations stay under this.
- **long (200/min)**: Overall quota limit. Prevents abuse even if requests are spread out over time.

All three limits apply simultaneously—violating ANY tier results in a 429 Too Many Requests response.

