**The design elegantly handles temporal queries without storing explicit snapshots**. Instead of maintaining pre-computed snapshots at every timestamp, the system uses a **write-only audit trail** (BarrelAudit) combined with window functions to reconstruct any historical state on-demand. The `ROW_NUMBER() OVER PARTITION BY barrel ORDER BY changedAt DESC` pattern is the key innovation—it ranks audit records efficiently without materializing intermediate results, allowing the database to scan just the necessary audit records up to the point-in-time and find the latest change per barrel in a single pass. The `COALESCE(audit_location, current_location)` logic cleverly handles the case where a barrel has never been moved (no audit record), defaulting to its current location. This approach trades CPU (for each query) to save storage (no snapshots), and the composite index on `[serialNumber, changedAt DESC]` ensures the queries remain performant even with large audit tables.
