### Memory & Performance Characteristics

- **File size limit**: 100MB (line 22 in service, line 312 in controller)
- **Batch size**: Configurable, typically 500-1000 rows per batch
- **Memory pattern**: Streaming avoids loading entire CSV into RAM; individual batches processed via SQL function
- **Progress tracking**: Database-backed metrics prevent loss of progress on restart
- **Safety monitoring**: Consecutive failures/empty batches trigger automatic halt

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
**Multi-Phase Streaming Design**: The pipeline separates concerns across distinct phases (validation → staging → processing) rather than doing all transformations in memory. This allows large files to be processed without memory pressure. CSV streaming via Transform streams (line 357) ensures row-by-row processing without buffering the entire file. The SQL function (process_inventory_batch) handles the complex business logic (lot lookup, cooperage parsing, barrel creation) at the database level, avoiding serialization overhead.

**Safety Limits as Circuit Breaker**: The system implements circuit breaker patterns (lines 127-158, 250-265) that stop processing if detecting consecutive empty batches or errors, preventing infinite loops on corrupted data. The distributed queue (line 350) allows pausing/resuming jobs without losing position, unlike recursion which would fail on large files.
