## Q83: How does the CachedEventTypeService optimize event type lookups? Describe the caching strategy and its impact on transaction performance.

**Answer:**

CachedEventTypeService implements **in-memory caching with distributed invalidation** to eliminate database query contention during high-concurrency Android sync processing. It solves the **TEC-611 problem** (SSI predicate locks on EventType lookups) by moving event type queries completely out of serializable transactions.

### Caching Strategy Architecture

The service at `apps/whk-wms/src/eventType/cached-event-type.service.ts:1-278` uses three data structures for efficient lookups:

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class CachedEventTypeService implements OnModuleInit {
  // In-memory cache: Map<eventTypeName, EventType | null>
  private eventTypeCache = new Map<string, EventType | null>();  // Line 26

  // Cache metadata: Map<eventTypeName, cacheTimestamp>
  private cacheTimestamps = new Map<string, number>();  // Line 29

  // Reverse index: Map<typeId, Set<eventTypeName>>
  // TEC-1196: Tracks ALL cache key variants (names) for each type ID for invalidation
  // Multiple name variants ("Entry", "ENTRY", "entry") map to the same EventType ID
  private idToNameMap = new Map<string, Set<string>>();  // Line 32-35

  // Cache TTL: 10 minutes (600,000 ms)
  private readonly CACHE_TTL_MS = 10 * 60 * 1000;  // Line 37

  // Redis pub/sub channel for distributed cache invalidation
  private readonly CACHE_INVALIDATION_CHANNEL = "cache:invalidate:event-type";  // Line 40
}
```

### Cache Lookup Logic with TTL

The `findEventTypeByName()` method at lines 99-141 implements a three-tier lookup strategy:

```typescript
async findEventTypeByName(name: string): Promise<EventType | null> {
  const now = Date.now();
  const cachedTimestamp = this.cacheTimestamps.get(name);

  // Tier 1: Check if cache entry exists and is still valid (within TTL)
  if (cachedTimestamp && now - cachedTimestamp < this.CACHE_TTL_MS) {
    const cached = this.eventTypeCache.get(name);
    this.logger.debug(`Cache HIT for EventType: ${name}`);
    return cached ?? null;  // Line 113: Return cached value (including null)
  }

  // Tier 2: Cache miss or expired - fetch from database
  // TEC-1196: EventTypeService.findEventTypeByName() handles normalization
  this.logger.debug(
    `Cache MISS for EventType: ${name}, fetching from database`,
  );
  const eventType = await this.eventTypeService.findEventTypeByName(name);  // Line 122

  // Tier 3: Update cache (store null results too to avoid repeated lookups)
  this.eventTypeCache.set(name, eventType);  // Line 126
  this.cacheTimestamps.set(name, now);  // Line 127

  // TEC-1196: Track ALL name variants for this event type ID for invalidation
  // Different case variations ("Entry", "ENTRY", "entry") all map to same EventType
  if (eventType) {
    if (!this.idToNameMap.has(eventType.id)) {
      this.idToNameMap.set(eventType.id, new Set());  // Line 132
    }
    this.idToNameMap.get(eventType.id)!.add(name);  // Line 134
  }

  return eventType;
}
```

