  private locationByStringCache = new Map<string, StorageLocation | null>();
  private cacheTimestamps = new Map<string, number>();
  private reverseIndex = new Map<string, Set<string>>(); // Reverse index for efficient multi-key invalidation
  ```
- **TTL**: Line 47: `private readonly CACHE_TTL_MS = 10 * 60 * 1000;`

**4. CachedLotVariationService** (`apps/whk-wms/src/lotVariation/cached-lot-variation.service.ts:1-330`)
- **TTL**: Line 40: `private readonly CACHE_TTL_MS = 10 * 60 * 1000;`

### **Two-Tier Invalidation Mechanism**

**Tier 1: TTL-Based Automatic Expiration** (Cache Miss Pattern)

Every `findXXX()` method checks TTL before returning cached values (`CachedStorageLocationService:90-106`):

```typescript
async findById(id: string): Promise<StorageLocation | null> {
  const now = Date.now();
  const cacheKey = `id:${id}`;
  const cachedTimestamp = this.cacheTimestamps.get(cacheKey);

  // Check if cache entry exists and is still valid (TTL check)
  if (cachedTimestamp && (now - cachedTimestamp) < this.CACHE_TTL_MS) {
    const cached = this.locationByIdCache.get(id);
    this.logger.debug(`Cache HIT for StorageLocation ID: ${id}`);
    return cached ?? null;
  }

  // Cache miss or expired - fetch from database
  this.logger.debug(`Cache MISS for StorageLocation ID: ${id}, fetching from database`);
  const location = await this.prisma.storageLocation.findUnique({
    where: { id },
    include: { warehouseConfig: true }
  });

  // Update cache (store null results too to avoid repeated lookups)
  this.locationByIdCache.set(id, location);
  this.cacheTimestamps.set(cacheKey, now);

  return location;
}
```

**Key Points:**
- Expired entries are **lazy-invalidated** on next access (no background cleanup thread)
- Null values are **cached** to prevent repeated database queries for non-existent items
- TTL is uniform: **10 minutes** across all cached services

**Tier 2: Distributed Invalidation via Redis pub/sub**

Public invalidation methods trigger both local and distributed updates (`CachedStorageLocationService:291-310`):

```typescript
/**
 * Invalidate cache for a specific location (public API)
 * Combines local invalidation + distributed notification
 */
invalidateLocation(locationId: string): void {
  this.performLocalInvalidation(locationId);      // Line 292
  this.emitDistributedInvalidation(locationId);   // Line 293
}

/**
 * Perform local cache invalidation for a specific location
 * Removes all cache entries related to the location using reverse index
 */
private performLocalInvalidation(locationId: string): void {
  // Get all cache keys associated with this location (via reverse index)
  const cacheKeys = this.reverseIndex.get(locationId);  // Line 299

  if (!cacheKeys || cacheKeys.size === 0) {
    this.logger.debug(`No cache entries found for location: ${locationId}`);
    return;
  }

  // Delete all associated cache entries
  for (const cacheKey of cacheKeys) {
    if (cacheKey.startsWith('id:')) {
      this.locationByIdCache.delete(locationId);  // Line 310
    } else {
      this.locationByStringCache.delete(cacheKey); // Line 312
    }
    this.cacheTimestamps.delete(cacheKey);         // Line 316
  }

  this.reverseIndex.delete(locationId);            // Line 319

  this.logger.debug(`Locally invalidated ${cacheKeys.size} cache entries for location: ${locationId}`);
}
```

**Distributed Notification** (`CachedStorageLocationService:322-344`):

```typescript
private async emitDistributedInvalidation(locationId: string): Promise<void> {
  if (!this.pubSubProvider) {
    return; // No Redis, skip distributed invalidation
  }

  try {
    const pubSub = this.pubSubProvider.getInstance();
    await pubSub.publish(this.CACHE_INVALIDATION_CHANNEL, {  // Line 331
      locationId,
      timestamp: Date.now(),
    });

    this.logger.debug(`Published distributed invalidation for location: ${locationId}`);
  } catch (error) {
    this.logger.error(
      `Failed to publish distributed invalidation for location ${locationId}: ${error}`,
    );
  }
}
```

**Receiving Invalidation Events** (`CachedStorageLocationService:347-356`):

```typescript
private handleDistributedInvalidation(event: {
  locationId: string;
  timestamp: number;
}): void {
  this.logger.debug(
    `Received distributed invalidation for location: ${event.locationId} (timestamp: ${event.timestamp})`,
  );

  // Perform local invalidation only (don't re-publish)
  this.performLocalInvalidation(event.locationId);  // Line 354
}
```

### **Reverse Index Pattern: Efficient Multi-Variant Invalidation**

The reverse index is crucial for handling multiple cache keys per entity (`CachedStorageLocationService:357-363`):

```typescript
private addToReverseIndex(locationId: string, cacheKey: string): void {
  if (!this.reverseIndex.has(locationId)) {
    this.reverseIndex.set(locationId, new Set());  // Line 359
  }
  this.reverseIndex.get(locationId)!.add(cacheKey);  // Line 361
}
```

**Why This Matters (TEC-1196 - Cache Name Variants):**

A single StorageLocation can be cached under **three different keys**:
- `id:locationId` (by primary key)
- `globalId:qrCode` (by QR code)
- `loc:warehouse:floor:tier:rick:position` (by physical location components)

Without reverse index, invalidating a location would require searching all three cache maps. With reverse index:
```
reverseIndex:
  locationId → {id:locationId, globalId:qrCode, loc:W:F:T:R:P}

When invalidating locationId:
  1. Look up reverseIndex.get(locationId) → returns all 3 keys
  2. Delete all 3 cache entries in one pass
```

### **Cache Warming Coordination**

All caches are warmed in parallel at application startup (`apps/whk-wms/src/androidSyncInbox/android-sync.processor.ts:100-109`):

```typescript
