### **Redis pub/sub Subscription Setup**

Each service subscribes to its invalidation channel during `onModuleInit()` (`CachedStorageLocationService:62-88`):

```typescript
async onModuleInit(): Promise<void> {
  if (!this.pubSubProvider) {
    this.logger.log('Skipping distributed cache subscription (no Redis)');
    return;
  }

  try {
    const pubSub = this.pubSubProvider.getInstance();
    const iterator = pubSub.asyncIterableIterator<{
      locationId: string;
      timestamp: number;
    }>(this.CACHE_INVALIDATION_CHANNEL) as AsyncIterableIterator<{
      locationId: string;
      timestamp: number;
    }>;

    // Background process to handle invalidation events (async, never blocks startup)
    (async () => {
      for await (const event of iterator) {
        this.handleDistributedInvalidation(event);
      }
    })().catch((error) => {
      this.logger.error(`Error processing cache invalidation events: ${error}`);
    });

    this.logger.log(
      `📡 Subscribed to distributed cache invalidation channel: ${this.CACHE_INVALIDATION_CHANNEL}`,
    );
  } catch (error) {
    this.logger.error(`Failed to subscribe to cache invalidation channel: ${error}`);
  }
}
```

**Key Design Choices:**
- Subscription runs in **background async** (doesn't block module initialization)
- Errors in subscription are logged but don't fail the application
- **Graceful degradation**: If Redis unavailable, caching still works with TTL-only invalidation

### **Lifecycle Management**

The `CachedEventReasonService` implements proper cleanup (`cached-event-reason.service.ts:10-12`):

