### **Error Categorization Pipeline** (`apps/whk-wms/src/inventory-upload/error-categorization.service.ts:58-95`)

Four-stage categorization flow:

**Stage 1: PostgreSQL Error Code Mapping** (lines 114-152)
```typescript
private categorizePostgreSQLError(error: PostgreSQLError): ErrorCategory | null {
  if (!error.code) return null;

  // Class 23: Integrity Constraint Violations
  if (code === "23503") return ErrorCategory.REFERENCE;  // Foreign key
  if (code === "23505") return ErrorCategory.REFERENCE;  // Unique
  if (code === "23514") return ErrorCategory.BUSINESS_RULE; // Check
  if (code === "23502") return ErrorCategory.VALIDATION; // Not null
```
Postgres error codes directly map to categories via code prefixes (08=SYSTEM, 22=VALIDATION, 23=constraints, 42=SYSTEM, 53=SYSTEM).

**Stage 2: Prisma Error Code Mapping** (lines 154-196)
```typescript
private categorizePrismaError(error: PrismaError): ErrorCategory | null {
  switch (code) {
    case "P2003": return ErrorCategory.REFERENCE;  // Foreign key
    case "P2005":
    case "P2006":
    case "P2007": return ErrorCategory.VALIDATION; // Invalid value
    case "P2011":
    case "P2012": return ErrorCategory.VALIDATION; // Null constraint
```
Prisma SDK error codes (P2xxx series) map to business categories.

**Stage 3: Business Rule Pattern Matching** (lines 198-260)
```typescript
private categorizeBusinessRuleError(error: BusinessRuleError): ErrorCategory | null {
  // Relocation-specific patterns
  if (errorType.includes("relocation:locationalreadyoccupied") || 
      (message.includes("relocating") && message.includes("already stored"))) {
    return ErrorCategory.BUSINESS_RULE;
  }

  // InventoryCheck patterns
  if (errorType.includes("inventorycheck:barrelhadpriorstorage")) {
    return ErrorCategory.BUSINESS_RULE;
  }
```
Domain-specific error type prefixes (Relocation:, InventoryCheck:, etc.) indicate business rule violations.

**Stage 4: Validation Pattern Fallback** (lines 262-284)
```typescript
private categorizeValidationError(message: string): ErrorCategory | null {
  const validationKeywords = [
    "invalid", "required", "missing", "empty", "null", "undefined",
    "format", "length", "range", "type", "validation", "must be",
    "should be", "expected", "cannot be", "not allowed", "not valid",
  ];

  if (validationKeywords.some((keyword) => lowerMessage.includes(keyword))) {
    return ErrorCategory.VALIDATION;
  }
}
```
Keyword-based fallback for unstructured error messages.

