### **Stage 3: Repair Reason Processing** (`apps/whk-wms/src/barrelEvent/barrelEvent.service.ts:2846-2901`)

This is the **core business logic**:

```typescript
private async processInspectionResult(
  tx: any,
  payload: InspectionPayload,
  data?: any,
) {
  // ★ KEY: Regex match for "pass" word boundary (case-insensitive)
  const containsPass =
    /\bpass\b/.exec(payload.repairReason?.toLowerCase()) !== null;

  let eventReasonConnect = undefined;
  let result = false;

  if (containsPass) {
    // Path A: If repairReason contains "pass" (case-insensitive)
    result = true;  // Inspection PASSED
    // NO eventReasonConnect - no failure reason
  } else {
    // Path B: If repairReason does NOT contain "pass" (failed inspection)
    if (payload && payload.repairReason) {
      // Look up EventReason record by name
      const eventReason = await tx.eventReason.findFirst({
        where: { name: payload.repairReason },  // EXACT name match
      });

      if (eventReason) {
        // Found repair reason in EventReason master table
        eventReasonConnect = { connect: { id: eventReason.id } };
      } else {
        // ★ CRITICAL: Repair reason not found in master data
        const errorToLog = {
          errorLevel: EnumDeviceSyncErrorLevel.ERROR,
          errorType: "EventReasonLogicNotFound",
          errorMessage: `EventReason not found for Inspection: ${payload.repairReason}`,
          context: {
            barrelSN: data?.barrelSN,
            locationString: data?.locationString,
            eventType: "Inspection",
            operator: data?.operator || "system",
            deviceName: data?.inboxDeviceName || data?.deviceName || "Not Available @ENT",
            originalPayload: {
              ...data,
              invalidEventReason: payload.repairReason,  // Capture attempted reason
            },
            inboxDeviceName: data?.inboxDeviceName || data?.deviceName,
            inboxId: data?.inboxId,
          },
        };

        // Attach error to exception for caller to log after transaction
        const exception = new NotFoundException(
          `EventReason not found for Inspection: ${payload.repairReason}`,
        );
        (exception as any).errorToLog = errorToLog;
        throw exception;  // Transaction rolls back
      }
    }
    result = false;  // Inspection FAILED
  }

  return { result, eventReasonConnect };  // Return both for persistence
}
```

**Three Decision Points**:

| Scenario | repairReason | result | eventReasonConnect | Meaning |
|----------|-------------|--------|-------------------|---------|
| **PASS** | "barrel looks good - PASS" | `true` | `undefined` | Inspection approved, no repair needed |
| **FAIL** | "Worm Holes --> Head" | `false` | `{ connect: { id: "..." } }` | Inspection failed, repair reason required |
| **FAIL UNKNOWN** | "BadCustomRepairReason" | `false` | `undefined` (error thrown) | Invalid repair reason, transaction rolls back |

**Regex Detail** (line 2853):
- Pattern: `/\bpass\b/` - word boundary match
- Case-insensitive (`.toLowerCase()`)
- Examples matching: `"PASS"`, `"Pass"`, `"barrel looks good - pass"`, `"Inspection Pass"`
- Examples NOT matching: `"password"`, `"passage"`, `"passthrough"`

