### **Layer 1: Pre-Transaction Status Check** (`apps/whk-wms/src/resolution/base/resolution.service.ts:595-614`)

```typescript
// 3. Validate device sync errors exist and are unresolved
this.logger.log('🔍 [ResolutionService] Checking device sync errors:', {
  requestedErrorIds: createResolutionDto.deviceSyncErrorIds,
  count: createResolutionDto.deviceSyncErrorIds.length
});

const deviceSyncErrors = await prisma.deviceSyncError.findMany({
  where: {
    id: { in: createResolutionDto.deviceSyncErrorIds },
  },
  select: { id: true, status: true, errorType: true },
});

this.logger.log('📋 [ResolutionService] Found device sync errors:', {
  foundCount: deviceSyncErrors.length,
  requestedCount: createResolutionDto.deviceSyncErrorIds.length,
  errors: deviceSyncErrors.map(e => ({ id: e.id, status: e.status, errorType: e.errorType }))
});

if (
  deviceSyncErrors.length !==
  createResolutionDto.deviceSyncErrorIds.length
) {
  const foundIds = deviceSyncErrors.map((e) => e.id);
  const missingIds = createResolutionDto.deviceSyncErrorIds.filter(
    (id) => !foundIds.includes(id),
  );
  this.logger.error('❌ [ResolutionService] Missing device sync errors:', {
    missingIds,
    foundIds
  });
  throw new NotFoundException(
    `Device sync errors not found: ${missingIds.join(", ")}`,
  );
}

// ★ CRITICAL CONCURRENCY CHECK: Reject if ANY errors already resolved
const alreadyResolvedErrors = deviceSyncErrors.filter(
  (error) => error.status === "RESOLVED",  // Line 611
);
if (alreadyResolvedErrors.length > 0) {
  this.logger.warn('⚠️ [ResolutionService] Some errors already resolved:', {
    alreadyResolvedIds: alreadyResolvedErrors.map((e) => e.id),
    allErrors: deviceSyncErrors.map(e => ({ id: e.id, status: e.status }))
  });
  throw new BadRequestException(
    `Some errors are already resolved: ${alreadyResolvedErrors.map((e) => e.id).join(", ")}`,
  );
}
```

**Key Design**:
- **Fail-fast strategy** (lines 611-614): Checks status field *before* entering transaction
- **Diagnostic logging** (lines 601-607): Logs all found errors with status for debugging
- **All-or-nothing semantics**: Rejects batch if *any* error is already RESOLVED
- **Prevents silent overwrites**: User sees which errors failed status check

