### Queue Health (MAX_ACTIVE_JOBS = 100): Permissive Monitoring

**`apps/whk-wms/src/inventory-upload/queue-health.service.ts:85-91, 160-162`**

```typescript
// Line 90: Used to determine overall health status
const isHealthy =
  queueStatuses.every((q) => q.isHealthy) &&
  overallFailureRate <= this.MAX_FAILURE_RATE &&
  totalActive <= this.MAX_ACTIVE_JOBS;  // 100 is acceptable for health

// Line 160-162: Report issue only if exceeding 100
if (activeCount > this.MAX_ACTIVE_JOBS) {
  issues.push(
    `Too many active jobs: ${activeCount} (max: ${this.MAX_ACTIVE_JOBS})`,
  );
}
```

**Why 100?**
- **Permissive threshold**: Allows queue to handle 10x more concurrent jobs before flagging as "unhealthy"
- **Reporting, not enforcement**: Only REPORTS status via `getOverallHealth()`, doesn't block operations
- **Part of larger health assessment**: Considered alongside failure rates (10%), failed job counts (50), waiting jobs (500)
- **Designed for operational visibility**: Operations team sees "warning" status at 100 active jobs, but system doesn't stop

---

### Supporting Context: Other Threshold Differences

**resource-monitor.service.ts: Very permissive for non-job metrics**

**`apps/whk-wms/src/inventory-upload/resource-monitor.service.ts:33-37`**
```typescript
